  "_comment": "Machine-readable FlashAttention (bf16, attn_npu2.o, seq-first builder attn_npu2_seqfirst.py) schedules on NPU2, read via kernel_registry/registry_lookup.py fa_config(). Keyed by the exact attention shape. schedule fields are build_launch kwargs; heads_rows > 1 puts head groups on the herd's rows (columns = (num_heads_per_unroll / heads_rows) * num_q_tiles <= 8, rows = heads_rows * num_cascade_stages <= 4); q_launch splits the q blocks over launch iterations to stay within 16 shim BDs. fused_merge needs attn_npu2.o built with fused_merge (-DFUSED_MERGE) and qk_pretranspose (-DQK_PRETRANSPOSE). latency is the whole call (all heads, all images), median of 3, turbo pmode. Measured 2026-10-14, main f9457c51. The fused_merge rows were measured with -DMAX_X4 as well, which measured at parity in the SmolVLA pipeline and is not part of the kernel.",
